 "root_cause": "A list refresh advanced the view epoch while retaining old detail/actions. A user could open archive confirmation against that old detail; the pending refresh then advanced the epoch again and the existing safety guard rejected confirmation. Two controlled runs kept the original assertion of1 option but observed2, current-record-changed and zero DELETE requests. A separate archived-detail branch cleared selection without removing the now-known archived row from cached choices.",
 "changes": [
  "Clear old row/preview/actions/attempts at list-read start, keeping the existing view/revision checks",
  "Remove a detail-confirmed archived choice when the current filter excludes archives",
  "Keep the original delivery scenario byte-identical, including assertions and timeouts",
  "Update all current cache imports to20261116v132 and current guide branch metadata to v2; stage only HEAD-derived metadata and owned changes"
 ],
 "limits": [
